/**
 * Demo-history seed: populates the app with ~6 months of believable
 * procurement activity so every role's screens (dashboard charts, queues,
 * All Requests, POs, Reports, Audit Trail) have real volume behind them.
 *
 * Everything is generated by walking each request through the SAME state
 * machine the app enforces (submit -> division -> finance -> PO -> delivered
 * -> closed, with rejections / returns / withdrawals along the way), writing
 * matching workflow_history + audit_log rows at each step. So the demo data
 * is indistinguishable from data created by clicking through the UI - the
 * audit trail, timelines and numbering all line up.
 *
 * Deterministic: a fixed PRNG seed + fixed row IDs. Re-running is a no-op
 * once seeded. Pass --reset to delete the generated rows and regenerate them
 * relative to today (handy before a demo so "this week" charts look fresh).
 *
 * Requires the base seed first:  npm run db:seed
 * Run with:                      npm run db:seed:demo  [-- --reset]
 * Keep it current later:         npm run db:seed:demo -- --roll-forward [out.sql]
 */
